# 7. Greeting command — bench/references.md §7:
#
#   bind line <- readline in print ("hello, " ++ line)
#
# A command that reads a line and greets whoever typed it. `>` is bind and
# lands in the binder-name slot; `=` steps into the command it sequences;
# `readline` is a completion candidate rather than a key, so it is spelled.

# bind line <- ⦇⦈ in ⦇⦈, naming the binder as it is created
>
l
i
n
e

# the first step: the completion commits `readline` as it is typed
